A data analyst wants to aggregate daily sales into monthly totals. Which query correctly truncates dates to the month level and sums the revenue?

(A) SELECT DATE_TRUNC('MONTH', sale_date) AS month, SUM(revenue) FROM sales GROUP BY month;
(B) SELECT MONTH(sale_date) AS month, SUM(revenue) FROM sales

A data analyst has a `sales` table with columns: product, quarter, revenue. The analyst wants to transform the data so each quarter becomes its own column. Which query achieves this?

(A) SELECT * FROM sales PIVOT (SUM(revenue) FOR quarter IN ('Q1', 'Q2', 'Q3', 'Q4'));
(B) SELECT product, Q1, Q2, Q3
